I saved the subject-fairness review to `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Druski/2026-09-23_210138/subject.md`. The draft's hash matched before I started, and I didn't open any of the other jurors' reviews.

**Verdict: revise.** Trust is strained, not broken. The review finds 2 blockers and 7 concerns.

**Strongest hit:** the lawsuit section's closing line, "The dismissal is procedural, and no court ruled on the merits. The August order is the closest thing to a finding the case produced, and it points his way." It doesn't claim he was cleared, and it doesn't leave the sexual-assault allegation hanging. The Mafiathon line "'That ain't no excuse' is ownership, said live and to the kid" is close behind.

**The two blockers:**
- **Mafiathon (fix first).** It sits under the answer to "Is Druski a good person?", the page's biggest search query. The draft judges him for never answering the boy's mother. It doesn't say that within three days she was publicly using racial slurs about him. It also leaves out that her complaint about security was aimed at the organizers of Kai Cenat's stream. The fix is one neutral, sourced sentence, or dropping that verdict. I confirmed the slurs report (Atlanta Black Star, Nov 30, 2024) only from its headline, so someone needs to open the article before it goes into the draft.
- **The 2022 skit.** In April 2022 Druski took down a skit after backlash. In 2024 he told Rolling Stone he "didn't want to continue to trigger people." The draft never mentions this. Meanwhile its search title ("the Critics He Ignores"), meta description, two FAQs and the Rabbit Hole's main argument against Type 3 all say he never backs down.

**Highest-priority concern:** the draft states guesses about his inner life as fact: "Anger is the Eight's fuel," "defiance with built-in deniability," and "Every laugh he chases now doubles as proof." On record, his own words are hurt, "I'ma prove it to y'all," and wanting to be "the funniest kid in the class." The draft also puts quotation marks around "I'm just joking," which he isn't recorded saying.

The fixes add roughly 90 words and the suggested cuts free more than that. That matters because the draft is about 6 words under its 3,900-word band.
